   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,176:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Manual text revisions, formatting changes, and image removal or replacement captures by @ABagram
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,178:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Tutorial 1: The battery
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,179:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Spintronic circuits are powered by a 
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,179:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: battery
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,182:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: . The battery pulls chains through circuits, just like electrical batteries
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,183:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: pull electrons through wires.
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,187:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <div style="text-align: center;"><img
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,191:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: src="https://i.imgur.com/nnQn38z.png" alt="Image" width="70%"
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,192:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: /></div>
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,193:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Pull the string back and let it fly
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,194:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: !
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,195:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  It got going too fast, didn
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,196:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,196:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: t it?
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,197:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Good thing I built a circuit breaker into it
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,198:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: !
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,199:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Try it again. This time, after you pull back the string, 
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,201:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: use your fingers to add some resistance to the output
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,201:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: sprockets
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,203:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: . Can you release all of the energy in the battery without triggering the circuit breaker?
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,204:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: From now on, we
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,205:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,206:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ll have to avoid 
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,206:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: shorts
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,207:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: !
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,218:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  A short is wherever the battery has a path to release its energy without any
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,221:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: resistance. How do you add resistance to the battery without using your fingers? With a resistor.
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,222:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: NEW PART UNLOCKED
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,225:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <div style="text-align: center;"><img
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,226:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: src="https://i.imgur.com/cpBhm2D.png" alt="Image" width="30%"
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,227:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: /></div>
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,228:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <p style="text-align: center;"><b>THE SPINTRONIC RESISTOR</b></p>
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,229:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: PURPOSE:
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,230:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: RESISTORS RESIST THE FLOW OF CHAIN.
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,231:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: DETAIL:
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,232:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: RESISTANCE IS MEASURED IN 
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,233:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,234:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: SPIN OHMS.
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,234:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,237:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  THE HIGHER THE SPIN OHM VALUE OF A RESISTOR,
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,238:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: THE HARDER IT IS TO TURN.
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,239:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: THE SYMBOL FOR A SPIN OHM IS 
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,240:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,241:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Ω
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,244:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,245:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Tutorial 2: Build a basic circuit
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,246:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Let
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,246:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,248:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s build a basic circuit with a resistor and a battery. Before we can build a circuit with a resistor, we
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,249:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,250:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ve got to
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,251:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: make the workspace bigger.
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,252:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Step 1.
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,254:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  Place a tile in front of the battery.
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,262:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <div style="text-align: center;"><img
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,272:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: src="https://pplines-online.bj.bcebos.com/deploy/official/paddleocr/pp-ocr-vl-16-online//c5b52f00-7cea-4746-93e7-962e2ebfbd7d/markdown_3/imgs/img_in_image_box_352_442_834_753.jpg?authorization=bce-auth-v1%2FALTAKDN8mY5KlNI7zaRpLmOqrw%2F2026-08-11T07%3A56%3A47Z%2F-1%2F%2F70201094b622c297eefcc6023e0182cf79e96bc462aaf2ee25a7e9da12a6ae38" alt="Image" width="40%" /></div>
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,273:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Step 2.
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,275:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  Put a tile connector in the hole between them and twist it a quarter turn using the tile connector tool.
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,285:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <div style="text-align: center;"><img
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,298:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: src="https://pplines-online.bj.bcebos.com/deploy/official/paddleocr/pp-ocr-vl-16-online//c5b52f00-7cea-4746-93e7-962e2ebfbd7d/markdown_3/imgs/img_in_image_box_139_963_559_1365.jpg?authorization=bce-auth-v1%2FALTAKDN8mY5KlNI7zaRpLmOqrw%2F2026-08-11T07%3A56%3A47Z%2F-1%2F%2F66ef6a50bcab46867d5900b76079939faa0edf7f19b4d84bd8af997489d26f33" alt="Image" width="35%" /></div>
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,307:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <div style="text-align: center;"><img
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,317:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: src="https://pplines-online.bj.bcebos.com/deploy/official/paddleocr/pp-ocr-vl-16-online//c5b52f00-7cea-4746-93e7-962e2ebfbd7d/markdown_3/imgs/img_in_image_box_621_936_1055_1367.jpg?authorization=bce-auth-v1%2FALTAKDN8mY5KlNI7zaRpLmOqrw%2F2026-08-11T07%3A56%3A47Z%2F-1%2F%2F25ecfa8b9c65a4995f34eef58c5ce254df8f61ecd3a68848785e76437effc228" alt="Image" width="36%" /></div>
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,318:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Step 3.
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,320:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  Connect the motor to a 500 Ω resistor with a loop of chain. Most parts have 3 levels. It doesn
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,321:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,325:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: t matter which
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,327:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: one you use, but chains must connect sprockets at the same level.
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,329:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <div style="text-align: center;"><img
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,331:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: src="https://i.imgur.com/coOgXb7.png" alt="Image" width="70%"
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,332:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: /></div>
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,333:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Step 4.
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,336:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  After you place a chain loop around sprockets, adjust the tension by sliding one part away from the other.
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,337:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: There should be just a tiny bit of slack in the chain
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,338:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: !
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,339:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: !
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,340:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  If it
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,341:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,342:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s too tight, it will add extra resistance. If it
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,344:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,345:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s too loose, the
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,346:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: chain will skip.
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,348:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Step 5.
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,349:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  Ok, we
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,350:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,351:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: re ready
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,352:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: !
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,353:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  Pull the string and let go. Our first circuit
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,354:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: !
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,355:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: HOW TO BUILD CHAINS
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,357:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Start by making 8 separate chain loops of about 40 links each. Pieces snap either direction
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,358:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: !
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,359:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: As you wrap the chain around sprockets to make circuits, add or remove links to shorten or lengthen the chain.
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,360:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Use the blue links to help you see the circuit
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,361:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,362:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s speed and direction.
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,365:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <div style="text-align: center;"><img
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,366:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: src="https://i.imgur.com/XPdaSSt.png" alt="Image" width="34%"
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,367:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: /></div>
