   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,555:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: DIFFICULTY: ★☆☆☆☆
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,571:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: CHALLENGE 4: CLOCKWISE AND COUNTERCLOCKWISE
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,573:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: MAKE ONE RESISTOR TURN CLOCKWISE WHILE THE OTHER TURNS COUNTERCLOCKWISE.
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,574:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: CLOCKWISE = ↻
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,575:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: COUNTERCLOCKWISE = ↺
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,576:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Counterclockwise?
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,576:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: !
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,577:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ?
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,578:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  How is that even possible? The battery turns 
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,579:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: clockwise
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,580:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: !
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,581:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: I guess we
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,582:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,582:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ll need to think 
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,583:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: outside the loop
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,584:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: .
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,585:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: STARTING SETUP
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,592:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <div style="text-align: center;"><img
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,601:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: src="https://pplines-online.bj.bcebos.com/deploy/official/paddleocr/pp-ocr-vl-16-online//788d1b0c-d5ac-4597-9749-bc8f5e3e9d85/markdown_0/imgs/img_in_image_box_212_836_551_1384.jpg?authorization=bce-auth-v1%2FALTAKDN8mY5KlNI7zaRpLmOqrw%2F2026-08-11T07%3A56%3A30Z%2F-1%2F%2F61344850098d45cdba4039b70bf876757d4f7aaa4307de839228ba215c96ba4c" alt="Image" width="28%" /></div>
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,602:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: AVAILABLE PARTS
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,603:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,604:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 1 × 1000 Ω
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,605:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,606:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 1 × Chain
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,606:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,607:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 1 × 500 Ω
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,608:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: DIFFICULTY: ★★☆☆☆
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,609:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: CHALLENGE 5: COUNTERCLOCKWISE ONLY
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,610:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: MAKE BOTH RESISTORS TURN COUNTERCLOCKWISE.
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,610:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: STARTING SETUP
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,618:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <div style="text-align: center;"><img
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,628:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: src="https://pplines-online.bj.bcebos.com/deploy/official/paddleocr/pp-ocr-vl-16-online//788d1b0c-d5ac-4597-9749-bc8f5e3e9d85/markdown_1/imgs/img_in_image_box_95_1068_757_1414.jpg?authorization=bce-auth-v1%2FALTAKDN8mY5KlNI7zaRpLmOqrw%2F2026-08-11T07%3A56%3A30Z%2F-1%2F%2F59adc5a63ad38bbff40b59ba56d9bc70efec732d92f7ceb416fb13d4de15ed48" alt="Image" width="55%" /></div>
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,629:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Hmm. Sometimes there are 
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,630:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: more parts
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,631:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  available than you actually 
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,632:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: need
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,633:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: .
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,635:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: AVAILABLE PARTS
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,636:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,637:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 1 × 1000 Ω
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,638:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,639:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 2 × Chain
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,639:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,640:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 1 × 500 Ω
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,641:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: DIFFICULTY: ★★☆☆☆
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,642:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Tutorial 3: Circuits
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,643:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Electronic circuits are always made of loops. A power station doesn
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,644:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,644:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: t 
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,645:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: make
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,652:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  electrons and send them to a house
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,654:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: through wires, it simply pushes and pulls the electrons that are already in the wires.
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,657:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <div style="text-align: center;"><img
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,659:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: src="https://i.imgur.com/F1WHiyq.png" alt="Image" width="70%"
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,659:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: /></div>
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,660:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: It
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,661:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,663:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s the same with spintronics. The spintronic battery doesn
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,664:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,665:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: t 
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,666:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: make
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,667:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  chain, it simply pulls a loop of chain around a
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,668:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: circuit.
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,669:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: What happens if you don
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,670:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,671:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: t make a loop?
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,674:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: In spintronics, the chain flies out onto the floor, and it eventually stops running. Luckily, in electronics, the electrons
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,675:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: don
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,676:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,681:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: t spill out onto the floor. That would leave a very dangerous situation in your house, and the power station
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,682:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: would run out of electrons to push
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,683:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: !
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,684:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: NEW PART UNLOCKED
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,692:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <div style="text-align: center;"><img
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,701:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: src="https://pplines-online.bj.bcebos.com/deploy/official/paddleocr/pp-ocr-vl-16-online//788d1b0c-d5ac-4597-9749-bc8f5e3e9d85/markdown_3/imgs/img_in_image_box_348_265_636_699.jpg?authorization=bce-auth-v1%2FALTAKDN8mY5KlNI7zaRpLmOqrw%2F2026-08-11T07%3A56%3A31Z%2F-1%2F%2F7279aee7626743085322a93e428ca9d48ab3fc15739f3efc266ab9622f1d2a24" alt="Image" width="24%" /></div>
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,702:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <p style="text-align: center;"><b>THE SPINTRONIC SWITCH</b></p>
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,703:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: PURPOSE:
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,704:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: A SWITCH IS LIKE A MASSIVE RESISTOR THAT YOU CAN TOGGLE ON AND OFF.
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,705:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: DETAIL:
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,711:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: WHEN THE SWITCH IS ON (PUSHED DOWN), IT HAS NO RESISTANCE. WHEN THE SWITCH IS OFF
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,712:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: (UP), IT HAS SUCH A HIGH RESISTANCE THAT YOU CAN
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,713:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,713:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: T EVEN TURN IT.
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,714:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: CHALLENGE 6: THE SWITCH
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,715:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: MAKE THE RESISTOR (R1) TURN ON AND OFF WITH A SWITCH.
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,723:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <div style="text-align: center;"><img
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,732:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: src="https://pplines-online.bj.bcebos.com/deploy/official/paddleocr/pp-ocr-vl-16-online//e6fb7cb1-b7d1-4156-aa72-88042cd255d4/markdown_0/imgs/img_in_image_box_201_946_541_1610.jpg?authorization=bce-auth-v1%2FALTAKDN8mY5KlNI7zaRpLmOqrw%2F2026-08-11T07%3A56%3A30Z%2F-1%2F%2F6b7c8d575740e279de10526bb674d2d1ab857999c1e58d10de6417391c16e779" alt="Image" width="28%" /></div>
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,733:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: AVAILABLE PARTS
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,734:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,735:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 1 × Chain
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,735:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,736:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 1 × Switch
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,737:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: DIFFICULTY: ★☆☆☆☆
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,738:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: CHALLENGE 7: A SWITCH IN THE LOOP
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,739:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: TURN THE RESISTOR (R1) ON AND OFF WITH A SWITCH.
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,747:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <div style="text-align: center;"><img
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,756:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: src="https://pplines-online.bj.bcebos.com/deploy/official/paddleocr/pp-ocr-vl-16-online//e6fb7cb1-b7d1-4156-aa72-88042cd255d4/markdown_1/imgs/img_in_image_box_202_891_633_1503.jpg?authorization=bce-auth-v1%2FALTAKDN8mY5KlNI7zaRpLmOqrw%2F2026-08-11T07%3A56%3A31Z%2F-1%2F%2F7573e0f01c11dc8d7bf3e21cb073ced1fd4ab09ce937df0c6e5bb3522fa4580c" alt="Image" width="36%" /></div>
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,757:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: AVAILABLE PARTS
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,758:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,758:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 1 × Chain
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,759:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,760:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 1 × Switch
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,761:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: DIFFICULTY: ★☆☆☆☆
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,761:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Tutorial 4: Chain Tension
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,762:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Spintronic circuits are 
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,763:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,764:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: analog.
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,765:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,766:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  What does that mean? Well, things that are analog are 
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,767:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: continuous
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,768:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: . For example,
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,769:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: take these graphs:
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,772:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <div style="text-align: center;"><img
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,773:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: src="https://i.imgur.com/PVwbnLi.png" alt="Image" width="70%"
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,774:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: /></div>
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,776:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Things that are analog could have an 
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,777:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: infinite number of possible values
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,779:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  (like the graph on the left). The opposite
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,780:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: of analog is 
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,780:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,781:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: digital.
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,781:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,782:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  Things that are digital can only have 
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,783:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: certain values
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,784:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  (like the graph on the right).
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,784:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Analog is pretty great, right?
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,785:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: !
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,786:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  The tricky part about things that are analog is that 
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,787:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: every little imperfection
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,799:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  affects it.
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,806:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: For example, the speed a spintronic resistor turns is affected by things like the temperature, air resistance, humidity,
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,807:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: physical imperfections, and other things you can
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,808:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,809:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: t easily control.
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,809:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Eventually, you
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,810:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,811:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ll learn ways to design circuits that can 
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,812:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: tolerate
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,812:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  imperfections, but for now, we
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,813:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,815:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: re going to focus on
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,816:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: one important thing that you can control: 
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,817:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <u>
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,818:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: chain tension
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,819:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: </u>
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,819:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: .
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,821:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Connect two switches together with chain, like this:
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,828:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <div style="text-align: center;"><img
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,836:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: src="https://pplines-online.bj.bcebos.com/deploy/official/paddleocr/pp-ocr-vl-16-online//e6fb7cb1-b7d1-4156-aa72-88042cd255d4/markdown_3/imgs/img_in_image_box_419_252_746_552.jpg?authorization=bce-auth-v1%2FALTAKDN8mY5KlNI7zaRpLmOqrw%2F2026-08-11T07%3A56%3A33Z%2F-1%2F%2Fccaf6e32f19ac45134ea19d7b07bd29f8b9d7551f31b0d8038afed1a349193a1" alt="Image" width="27%" /></div>
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,838:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: First, gently slide the switches 
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,839:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: away
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,846:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  from each other so that the chain is tight. Make sure both switches are ON, and
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,847:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: then spin the switches with your finger. Do the switches spin freely?
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,855:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <div style="text-align: center;"><img
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,863:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: src="https://pplines-online.bj.bcebos.com/deploy/official/paddleocr/pp-ocr-vl-16-online//e6fb7cb1-b7d1-4156-aa72-88042cd255d4/markdown_3/imgs/img_in_image_box_393_769_775_887.jpg?authorization=bce-auth-v1%2FALTAKDN8mY5KlNI7zaRpLmOqrw%2F2026-08-11T07%3A56%3A33Z%2F-1%2F%2F6d8ace06120c5b208cbffa00a76be4fb38dc2d2f26a3f93cb320dfdc92316615" alt="Image" width="32%" /></div>
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,865:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Second, slide one switch just a tiny bit 
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,866:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: toward
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,867:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  the other so that the chain has just a 
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,867:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: little bit of slack
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,870:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: . Now spin the
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,872:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: switches with your finger. Do they spin freely now?
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,880:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <div style="text-align: center;"><img
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,888:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: src="https://pplines-online.bj.bcebos.com/deploy/official/paddleocr/pp-ocr-vl-16-online//e6fb7cb1-b7d1-4156-aa72-88042cd255d4/markdown_3/imgs/img_in_image_box_430_1127_737_1249.jpg?authorization=bce-auth-v1%2FALTAKDN8mY5KlNI7zaRpLmOqrw%2F2026-08-11T07%3A56%3A33Z%2F-1%2F%2F3e3509d32375d95305003cad4884f654afb6e4a858be85d933f14de74999eafd" alt="Image" width="25%" /></div>
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,890:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: When chains are tight, they add a lot of resistance. Make sure you leave 
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,891:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <u>
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,892:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: just a little bit of slack
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,893:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: </u>
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,894:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  when
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,895:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: you connect parts together.
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,896:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: CHALLENGE 8: THE 
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,897:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,898:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: AND
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,899:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,899:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  GATE
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,901:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: BUILD A CIRCUIT THAT TURNS THE RESISTOR ONLY WHEN BOTH SWITCHES S1 AND S2 ARE ON.
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,904:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <div style="text-align: center;"><img
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,906:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: src="https://i.imgur.com/GVxUFDN.png" alt="Image" width="48%"
