   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,908:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: STARTING SETUP
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,916:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <div style="text-align: center;"><img
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,925:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: src="https://pplines-online.bj.bcebos.com/deploy/official/paddleocr/pp-ocr-vl-16-online//ff34e5c3-7f56-49a8-96e7-274b031db228/markdown_0/imgs/img_in_image_box_221_877_550_1443.jpg?authorization=bce-auth-v1%2FALTAKDN8mY5KlNI7zaRpLmOqrw%2F2026-08-11T07%3A56%3A47Z%2F-1%2F%2Fd88f4be1359a40efeaa02b29f7fccee375e2c7a6b03f3190ae64f519f6beefea" alt="Image" width="27%" /></div>
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,927:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: AVAILABLE PARTS
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,928:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,929:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 1 × 500 Ω
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,929:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,930:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 3 × Chain
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,931:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: DIFFICULTY: ★☆☆☆☆
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,933:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Tutorial 5: Current
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,934:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: How fast does electricity flow through wires? Incredibly fast, right?
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,935:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: !
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,936:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  NOPE
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,937:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: !
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,938:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  Electrons move more like the chains in
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,938:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: spintronics.
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,945:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: How is that possible? Well imagine a long tube full of marbles. If you push a marble into one end, a marble pops out
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,946:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: the other end immediately, even though the marbles aren
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,947:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,947:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: t moving very fast.
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,950:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <div style="text-align: center;"><img
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,953:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: src="https://i.imgur.com/8otYgN7.png" alt="Image" width="80%"
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,954:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: /></div>
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,955:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: It
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,956:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,963:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s the same with electrons in wires. Signals travel fast through wires, but only because the wires are already full of
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,965:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: electrons. Spintronic chains do this, too
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,966:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: !
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,970:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  If you pull one end of a long chain, the other end moves immediately, even
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,972:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: though the chains aren
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,973:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,974:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: t moving very fast.
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,977:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <div style="text-align: center;"><img
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,978:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: src="https://i.imgur.com/9qefx6b.png" width="70%" /></div>
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,980:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The movement of chain (or electrons) through a circuit is called 
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,981:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,982:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: current.
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,983:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,992:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  A fast moving chain has high current.
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,994:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Current is measured in spin amps. The symbol for a spin amp is 
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,995:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,996:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: A.
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,997:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:23,999:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: How fast is a spin amp? A chain traveling at 0.001 A moves this far each second: |-----|
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,000:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: NEW PART UNLOCKED
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,010:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <div style="text-align: center;"><img
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,021:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: src="https://pplines-online.bj.bcebos.com/deploy/official/paddleocr/pp-ocr-vl-16-online//ff34e5c3-7f56-49a8-96e7-274b031db228/markdown_2/imgs/img_in_image_box_307_251_660_774.jpg?authorization=bce-auth-v1%2FALTAKDN8mY5KlNI7zaRpLmOqrw%2F2026-08-11T07%3A56%3A48Z%2F-1%2F%2F0a3131e3054653491dded94a504c437049cc622551290019a47a1acc1f524f10" alt="Image" width="29%" /></div>
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,023:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <p style="text-align: center;"><b>THE SPINTRONIC AMMETER</b></p>
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,023:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: PURPOSE:
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,027:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: THE AMMETER INDICATES THE AMOUNT OF CURRENT RUNNING THROUGH IT BY THE VOLUME
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,028:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: AND PITCH OF THE SOUND IT MAKES.
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,029:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: IT
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,030:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,031:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: S MOST USEFUL WITH HIGHER CURRENTS THAT YOU CAN
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,032:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,033:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: T EASILY SEE WITH YOUR EYES.
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,034:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: CHALLENGE 9: MAKE SOME NOISE
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,035:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: MAKE THE AMMETER A1 TURN.
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,038:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: NOTE: THE AMMETER HAS VERY LITTLE RESISTANCE, SO MAKE SURE YOU USE A RESISTOR TO
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,038:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: AVOID A SHORT
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,039:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: !
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,040:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: STARTING SETUP
