   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,178:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Tutorial 6: Circuit Diagrams
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,179:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Ugh. I need a better way to draw these spintronic circuits. It
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,179:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,181:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s too much work to draw pictures of all the sprockets
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,182:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: and chain.
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,183:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Maybe I can use electronic circuit symbols. Let
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,184:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,186:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s see...
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,188:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <div style="text-align: center;"><img
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,189:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: src="https://i.imgur.com/nCM7YEN.png" width="70%" /></div>
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,190:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ...and the chains are just like wires
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,191:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: !
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,192:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  So a simple circuit like this:
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,194:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <div style="text-align: center;"><img
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,195:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: src="https://i.imgur.com/a5j5ZsC.png" width="70%" /></div>
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,196:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: That
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,196:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,197:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s WAY easier
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,198:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: !
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,198:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  And we
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,199:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,200:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ll say the 
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,200:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,201:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: +
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,202:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,203:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  symbol on the battery is where it
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,204:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,205:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s 
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,205:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <u>
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,206:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: pushing
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,207:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: </u>
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,207:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  chain and the 
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,208:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,209:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: −
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,209:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,210:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  is
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,211:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: where it
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,211:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,212:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s 
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,213:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <u>
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,214:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: pulling
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,214:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: </u>
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,215:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  chain.
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,217:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Wait a second. What about these? How can we draw circuit diagrams for them?
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,218:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <div style="text-align: center;"><img
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,220:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: src="https://i.imgur.com/4WeWXzG.png" width="80%"/></div>
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,221:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: They
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,221:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,222:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: re all the same circuit
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,223:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: !
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,225:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  In each case, the resistors and battery are directly connected together. In other words,
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,226:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: you can
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,227:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,228:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: t turn one without turning the others
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,228:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: !
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,229:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,230:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <u>
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,232:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Any parts that are connected directly together must be drawn in
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,233:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: the same loop.
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,234:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: </u>
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,235:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  Like this:
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,243:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <div style="text-align: center;"><img
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,252:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: src="https://pplines-online.bj.bcebos.com/deploy/official/paddleocr/pp-ocr-vl-16-online//a9d7f43b-ba0c-4edd-83c9-eca63658a783/markdown_0/imgs/img_in_image_box_406_880_759_1121.jpg?authorization=bce-auth-v1%2FALTAKDN8mY5KlNI7zaRpLmOqrw%2F2026-08-11T07%3A56%3A30Z%2F-1%2F%2Fb8fdb2973280041e43169db66dca3071138899e708ef6e62116a94e8c43a5f40" alt="Image" width="40%" /></div>
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,253:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: It doesn
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,254:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,255:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: t matter what order you draw the parts in the diagram, they just have to be in the same loop.
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,256:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: CHALLENGE 13: FIRST CIRCUIT DIAGRAM
