   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,690:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: time Chain
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,691:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,691:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 1 × Junction
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,692:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: DIFFICULTY: ★★★☆☆
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,693:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Tutorial 10: Parallel circuits
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,695:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Are you starting to get the hang of junctions? Before junctions, everything was connected in 
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,696:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: series
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,702:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: : If one part turns,
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,704:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: the other parts turn. But when you put a junction between parts, they are connected in 
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,705:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,706:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: parallel
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,706:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,707:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: : turning one part
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,708:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: doesn
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,709:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,710:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: t necessarily make other parts turn.
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,711:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Here
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,711:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,713:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s a series circuit and a parallel circuit with two resistors:
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,716:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <div style="text-align: center;"><img
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,718:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: src="https://i.imgur.com/DQXV51f.png" alt="Image" width="70%"
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,719:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: /></div>
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,720:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: It
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,721:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,721:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s called 
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,722:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,722:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: parallel
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,723:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,724:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  because the junction splits the current between two circuits that run independently, or 
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,725:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,725:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: in
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,726:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: parallel
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,726:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,727:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: , with each other.
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,727:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Try it
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,728:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: !
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,730:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  Build each circuit. If you stop one resistor with your fingers, what happens to the other resistor?
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,731:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: CHALLENGE 20: WHERE IS THE HIGHEST CURRENT?
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:24,739:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: BUILD THE CIRCUIT BELOW. THEN ADD THE AMMETER AT THE LOCATION WITH THE HIGHEST
