   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,658:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Tutorial 16: Junction Spin Direction
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,659:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: In the remaining puzzles, we
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,660:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,662:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: re going to explore some unique things you can do with spintronics, but can
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,662:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,666:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: t do with
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,667:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: electronics. These useful tricks can often help you make simpler circuits
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,668:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: !
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,670:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Now you might have already noticed that 
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,672:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: junctions don
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,673:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,674:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: t always turn the way you
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,675:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,676:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: d expect
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,677:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: . For example:
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,684:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <div style="text-align: center;"><img
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,695:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: src="https://pplines-online.bj.bcebos.com/deploy/official/paddleocr/pp-ocr-vl-16-online//d5ce1f0d-0d17-4a55-a839-c09b5c68c62e/markdown_3/imgs/img_in_image_box_138_571_487_1054.jpg?authorization=bce-auth-v1%2FALTAKDN8mY5KlNI7zaRpLmOqrw%2F2026-08-11T07%3A56%3A39Z%2F-1%2F%2F0c81cfb63a8e3d80737e5ae24eb2c902dc9b58b894276f783b48fec2dfdd817b" alt="Image" width="29%" /></div>
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,697:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: In this circuit, the battery turns clockwise and so do R1 and R2.
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,706:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <div style="text-align: center;"><img
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,715:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: src="https://pplines-online.bj.bcebos.com/deploy/official/paddleocr/pp-ocr-vl-16-online//d5ce1f0d-0d17-4a55-a839-c09b5c68c62e/markdown_3/imgs/img_in_image_box_621_570_989_1056.jpg?authorization=bce-auth-v1%2FALTAKDN8mY5KlNI7zaRpLmOqrw%2F2026-08-11T07%3A56%3A40Z%2F-1%2F%2F6d8dccd2f2ea112a3c6e5db788fdeef3b031c5915476569e5b721167b23d7d02" alt="Image" width="30%" /></div>
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,716:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: In this circuit, the battery and R1 turn clockwise, 
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,717:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: but R2 turns counterclockwise.
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,726:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The difference is that in the first circuit, the battery applies voltage to the bottom sprocket, and in the second circuit,
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,727:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: the battery applies voltage to the middle sprocket.
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,730:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: If you apply voltage to one sprocket of a junction, how do you know which way it will push the other sprockets?
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,731:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Here
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,731:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,732:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s how you can figure it out:
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,735:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <div style="text-align: center;"><img
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,738:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: src="https://i.imgur.com/T0dN1ig.png" alt="Image" width="69%"
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,739:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: /></div>
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,746:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: First, look at the picture and find the sprocket you are applying a voltage to (like with the battery). Then follow the
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,747:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: arrows to the other sprockets. If it
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,748:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,749:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s a green arrow, it will push that sprocket with the 
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,750:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: same
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,751:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  voltage. If it
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,753:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,756:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s a red
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,757:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: arrow, it will push it with the 
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,758:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: opposite
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,759:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  voltage.
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,761:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: For example, if you apply a voltage to the middle sprocket, it pushes on the bottom sprocket in the 
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,762:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: same
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,764:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  direction,
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,766:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: but it pushes on the top sprocket in the 
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,767:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: opposite
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,777:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  direction. Or if you apply a voltage to the bottom sprocket, it
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,779:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: pushes on the middle sprocket in the same direction and the top sprocket in the 
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,780:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: same
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,781:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  direction.
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,782:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: CHALLENGE 52: JUNCTION SPIN DIRECTION
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,783:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: R1 MUST TURN COUNTERCLOCKWISE AND R2 MUST TURN CLOCKWISE.
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,784:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: STARTING SETUP
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,793:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <div style="text-align: center;"><img
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,802:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: src="https://pplines-online.bj.bcebos.com/deploy/official/paddleocr/pp-ocr-vl-16-online//56774bc1-fc58-4aca-bc63-5637aeae31d7/markdown_1/imgs/img_in_image_box_121_960_761_1545.jpg?authorization=bce-auth-v1%2FALTAKDN8mY5KlNI7zaRpLmOqrw%2F2026-08-11T07%3A56%3A32Z%2F-1%2F%2Fcdad8a53dcdf773cbe44ab11e3536cf48431c3c9ea95fb3586be4efde55d1b41" alt="Image" width="53%" /></div>
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,804:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: AVAILABLE PARTS
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,805:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,806:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 3 
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,806:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: \
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,807:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: times Chain
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,808:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: DIFFICULTY: ★★☆☆☆
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,809:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: CHALLENGE 53: JUNCTION SPIN DIRECTION 2
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,810:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: R1 AND R2 MUST BOTH TURN CLOCKWISE.
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,810:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: STARTING SETUP
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,818:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <div style="text-align: center;"><img
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,828:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: src="https://pplines-online.bj.bcebos.com/deploy/official/paddleocr/pp-ocr-vl-16-online//56774bc1-fc58-4aca-bc63-5637aeae31d7/markdown_2/imgs/img_in_image_box_26_960_690_1543.jpg?authorization=bce-auth-v1%2FALTAKDN8mY5KlNI7zaRpLmOqrw%2F2026-08-11T07%3A56%3A33Z%2F-1%2F%2F83db4b06270d42b39be0e49bf3398f9034c6687dc7749f72a8d7de22986cee85" alt="Image" width="55%" /></div>
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,829:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: AVAILABLE PARTS
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,830:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,830:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 3 
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,831:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: \
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,832:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: times Chain
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,832:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: DIFFICULTY: ★★☆☆☆
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,833:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: CHALLENGE 54: LOCKED CIRCUIT
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,835:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: BUILD A CIRCUIT THAT MAKES THE BATTERY UNABLE TO TURN.
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,836:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: STARTING SETUP
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,845:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <div style="text-align: center;"><img
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,854:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: src="https://pplines-online.bj.bcebos.com/deploy/official/paddleocr/pp-ocr-vl-16-online//56774bc1-fc58-4aca-bc63-5637aeae31d7/markdown_3/imgs/img_in_image_box_280_923_614_1520.jpg?authorization=bce-auth-v1%2FALTAKDN8mY5KlNI7zaRpLmOqrw%2F2026-08-11T07%3A56%3A33Z%2F-1%2F%2Ff5ebb09fef76b8551d8a26c7b94de3df934fa13369fef21b12f57a9d4afba3f1" alt="Image" width="28%" /></div>
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,855:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: AVAILABLE PARTS
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,856:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,857:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 1 
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,858:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: \
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,858:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: times 200 Ohm
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,859:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,860:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 3 
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,860:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: \
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,861:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: times Chain
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,862:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: DIFFICULTY: ★★☆☆☆
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,863:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Tutorial 17: Junction Dot Diagrams
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,864:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: It
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,864:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,865:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s pretty clear that the three sprockets of a junction aren
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,866:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,867:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: t exactly the same. We
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,868:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,871:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ll need a way to indicate which
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,873:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: sprocket is which on our diagrams.
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,874:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Here
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,874:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,875:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s a junction:
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,878:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <div style="text-align: center;"><img
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,879:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: src="https://i.imgur.com/xO24R7I.png" alt="Image" width="10%"
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,880:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: /></div>
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,881:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Let
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,881:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,882:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s mark the branch that
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,883:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,884:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s atached to the bottom sprocket of the junction with a little dot, like this:
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,888:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <div style="text-align: center;"><img
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,890:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: src="https://i.imgur.com/oSHkZvR.png" alt="Image" width="70%"
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,892:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: /></div>
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,893:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Now, when you
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,894:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,896:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: re trying to figure out which way a voltage will push on a branch, take your finger and trace the
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,897:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: path. 
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,898:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: If it passes a dot, the voltage will push the 
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,899:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <u>
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,900:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: same
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,901:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: </u>
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,903:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  direction through the branch. Otherwise, it
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,905:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: will push the 
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,906:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <u>
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,907:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: oppposite
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,907:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: </u>
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,908:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  direction.
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,910:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: For example, in this circuit, start by tracing the branch to the right. It passes a dot, so the voltage pushes in the same
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,911:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: direction.
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,913:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <div style="text-align: center;"><img
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,914:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: src="https://i.imgur.com/8fjfVkY.png" width="40%"/></div>
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,915:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Now trace the branch to the left. It does not pass a dot, so the voltage pushes in the opposite direction.
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,917:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <div style="text-align: center;"><img
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,918:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: src="https://i.imgur.com/8l7bBx1.png" width="40%"/></div>
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,931:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Here's the same basic circuit, but this time the battery is
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,937:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: connected to the bottom sprocket. Now both branches pass a dot, so
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,939:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: the voltage pushes in the same direction for both.
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,941:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <div style="text-align: center;"><img
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,943:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: src="https://i.imgur.com/pKQvV0R.png" width="40%"/></div>
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,945:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Notice I didn't draw a dot where the branches come back together. I
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,946:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: could, but it's unnecessary.
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,947:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Let
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,947:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,948:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s practice...
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,949:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: CHALLENGE 55: JUNCTION DOT DIAGRAMS 1
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,950:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: BUILD THE FOLLOWING CIRCUIT:
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,959:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <div style="text-align: center;"><img
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,967:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: src="https://pplines-online.bj.bcebos.com/deploy/official/paddleocr/pp-ocr-vl-16-online//e2788272-0d9a-4e5b-9be0-111650f1b3b2/markdown_2/imgs/img_in_image_box_35_167_334_469.jpg?authorization=bce-auth-v1%2FALTAKDN8mY5KlNI7zaRpLmOqrw%2F2026-08-11T07%3A56%3A34Z%2F-1%2F%2Fdbba77dc3d5b33449f9ec1b7640306cb203d1c3ae6c73c656b7453e331867d0b" alt="Image" width="30%" /></div>
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,969:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: IF CORRECT:
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,972:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <div style="text-align: center;"><img
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,973:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: src="https://i.imgur.com/QbeFIwg.png" width="20%"/></div>
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,974:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: (S)
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,975:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: STARTING SETUP
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,977:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <div style="text-align: center;"><img
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,979:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: src="https://i.imgur.com/parBLhC.png" alt="Image" width="56%"
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,980:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: /></div>
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,981:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: AVAILABLE PARTS
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,982:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,982:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 5 
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,983:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: \
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,984:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: times Chain
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,985:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: DIFFICULTY: ★★★☆☆
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,986:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: CHALLENGE 56: JUNCTION DOT DIAGRAMS 2
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,988:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: BUILD THE FOLLOWING CIRCUIT:
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,990:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <div style="text-align: center;"><img
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,992:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: src="https://i.imgur.com/ZGvPhXM.png" alt="Image" width="30%"
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,993:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: /></div>
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,993:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: IF CORRECT:
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,996:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <div style="text-align: center;"><img
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,997:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: src="https://i.imgur.com/vQupcpC.png" alt="Image" width="20%"
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,998:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: /></div>
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,998:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: (S)
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:26,999:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: STARTING SETUP
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,002:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <div style="text-align: center;"><img
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,004:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: src="https://i.imgur.com/qKagY1K.png" alt="Image" width="40%"
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,005:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: /></div>
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,006:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: AVAILABLE PARTS
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,007:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,007:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 5 
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,008:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: \
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,009:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: times Chain
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,009:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: DIFFICULTY: ★★★☆☆
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,010:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: CHALLENGE 57: ALL THE SAME DIRECTION
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,012:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: BUILD A CIRCUIT WHERE ALL THREE RESISTORS ARE IN PARALLEL AND THEY ALL TURN
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,013:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: CLOCKWISE.
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,014:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: A switch?
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,015:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: !
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,015:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ? Oh yeah
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,016:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: !
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,017:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  Sometimes I need a switch left in the ON position to change levels.
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,018:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: STARTING SETUP
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,022:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <div style="text-align: center;"><img
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,024:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: src="https://i.imgur.com/eUS6JAv.png" alt="Image" width="40%"
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,025:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: /></div>
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,025:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: AVAILABLE PARTS
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,026:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,027:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 6 
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,027:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: \
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,028:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: times Chain
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,029:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,029:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 1 
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,030:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: \
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,031:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: times Switch
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,032:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: DIFFICULTY: ★★★☆☆
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,033:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Tutorial 18: Spintronic Coupling
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,047:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Most spintronic parts have three sprockets that are joined together. Take the resistor, for instance. All three
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,049:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: sprockets are joined, so that if one moves, the other two also move. We say that 
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,050:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: chains attached to joined
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,052:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: sprockets are 
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,053:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,054:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: coupled
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,056:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,056:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  together.
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,064:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <div style="text-align: center;"><img
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,074:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: src="https://pplines-online.bj.bcebos.com/deploy/official/paddleocr/pp-ocr-vl-16-online//522f3264-ab6b-4121-850a-79aaef04f5ec/markdown_1/imgs/img_in_image_box_418_447_663_760.jpg?authorization=bce-auth-v1%2FALTAKDN8mY5KlNI7zaRpLmOqrw%2F2026-08-11T07%3A56%3A33Z%2F-1%2F%2Ffea5c0e0015d974251c61f04817e21913869344ffc426a7de73daaf660c2dbe1" alt="Image" width="20%" /></div>
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,075:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: It might not seem like much, but there
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,076:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,076:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s nothing quite like that in electronics, and it
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,077:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,078:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s 
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,078:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: powerful
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,079:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: . Eventually you
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,080:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,080:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ll see
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,081:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: why.
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,081:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: First, let
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,082:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,083:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s figure out how to diagram 
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,083:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,084:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: coupled
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,085:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,086:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  chains. Here
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,087:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,089:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s a series circuit with two resistors:
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,097:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <div style="text-align: center;"><img
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,106:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: src="https://pplines-online.bj.bcebos.com/deploy/official/paddleocr/pp-ocr-vl-16-online//522f3264-ab6b-4121-850a-79aaef04f5ec/markdown_1/imgs/img_in_image_box_322_1082_781_1478.jpg?authorization=bce-auth-v1%2FALTAKDN8mY5KlNI7zaRpLmOqrw%2F2026-08-11T07%3A56%3A33Z%2F-1%2F%2F9fc715c5b197bbc299d62112bb6c8ad7595c822a583954896ee33c7832194c42" alt="Image" width="38%" /></div>
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,107:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: And here
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,108:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,108:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s how we
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,109:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,110:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ve been drawing the circuit diagram for that circuit:
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,118:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <div style="text-align: center;"><img
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,128:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: src="https://pplines-online.bj.bcebos.com/deploy/official/paddleocr/pp-ocr-vl-16-online//522f3264-ab6b-4121-850a-79aaef04f5ec/markdown_2/imgs/img_in_image_box_575_173_940_425.jpg?authorization=bce-auth-v1%2FALTAKDN8mY5KlNI7zaRpLmOqrw%2F2026-08-11T07%3A56%3A33Z%2F-1%2F%2F3c42819676eb62a93f50f02099e4e5015158db792b7eb423d1f99721e9bef4ff" alt="Image" width="30%" /></div>
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,129:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: But technically, this is the correct way to draw it:
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,132:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <div style="text-align: center;"><img
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,134:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: src="https://i.imgur.com/7QVRD0C.png" alt="Image" width="60%"
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,134:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: /></div>
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,136:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The top chain loop turns because it
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,138:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,139:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s 
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,139:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,140:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: coupled
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,141:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,148:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  to the bottom chain loop at the 1000 Ohm resistor. That dashed line
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,149:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: between the 1000 Ohm resistor and the top loop tells us that 
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,150:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: both loops wrap around that resistor
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,152:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: . Of course, that
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,154:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: means the current in each loop 
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,155:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: must be the same
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,156:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: .
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,157:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Now, do you see those two dots next to the coupling? Since they
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,158:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,159:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: re both on the 
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,160:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: same end
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,162:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  of the coupling, they tell
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,163:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: us that both chains turn the 
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,164:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: same direction
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,165:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  around the resistor (clockwise).
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,166:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Now you
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,166:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,167:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: re probably thinking, 
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,168:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,171:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Are you crazy? Why not just draw it like the first diagram - it
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,172:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,173:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s waууy simpler
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,174:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: !
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,175:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,184:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  Well,
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,189:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: yeah, in this case, the first diagram is much simpler, and you can just draw it that way, but sometimes you have to
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,190:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: draw the coupling.
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,191:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: For instance, here the two loops are 
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,193:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: coupled oppositely
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,197:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: . The positive current through the resistor of the bottom loop
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,198:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: becomes a negative current through the top loop.
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,201:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <div style="text-align: center;"><img
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,205:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: src="https://i.imgur.com/opv3cTS.png" alt="Image" width="40%"
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,207:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: /></div>
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,210:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The corresponding circuit diagram looks like this:
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,224:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <div style="text-align: center;"><img
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,238:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: src="https://pplines-online.bj.bcebos.com/deploy/official/paddleocr/pp-ocr-vl-16-online//522f3264-ab6b-4121-850a-79aaef04f5ec/markdown_3/imgs/img_in_image_box_268_941_482_1434.jpg?authorization=bce-auth-v1%2FALTAKDN8mY5KlNI7zaRpLmOqrw%2F2026-08-11T07%3A56%3A34Z%2F-1%2F%2F28e4bafeb2175ee2d3202ecae7281cf649bcf84e6dbe8aa27e8dd9c6c42e4962" alt="Image" width="20%" /></div>
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,240:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Notice that the two dots are drawn on 
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,241:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: opposite ends
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,242:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  to indicate the 
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,243:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: opposite coupling
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,244:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: .
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,255:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: One more thing: You can couple circuit loops at other parts, too. Not just resistors, but also ammeters, switches,
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,256:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: capacitors, and even the battery. Here, two circuit loops are 
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,258:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: oppositely coupled at a switch
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,259:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: :
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,261:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <div style="text-align: center;"><img
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,263:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: src="https://i.imgur.com/PXYq8SU.png" alt="Image" width="70%"
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,264:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: /></div>
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,265:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: There
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,266:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,267:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s only one part you can
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,268:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,269:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: t directly couple to: the junction. That
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,270:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,271:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s because it doesn
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,272:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,284:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: t have any joined sprockets at
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,287:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: all. Still, if you need to, you can always connect the junction to another part (like a switch) and couple to that part
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,288:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: instead.
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,289:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Enough talk about coupling, 
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,289:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: let
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,291:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,291:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s try it out
   DEBUG: 2026-08-12 00:22:27,292:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: !
